      "prompt": "Continue to confirm the invariant at the end.",
      "learnerAction": "continue"
    }
  ],
  "narration": [
    {
      "at": 0.7,
      "text": "Seven sorted values: 3, 8, 12, 19, 23, 31, 40. The shaded window starts as the whole array."
    },
    {
      "at": 2.2,
      "text": "Probe the middle of the window: index 3 holds 19. Nineteen is smaller than the target 23."
    },
    {
      "at": 4.4,
      "text": "So the cells at or left of 19 are discarded and lo jumps to index 4. The window is cells 4 to 6, and 23 is still inside it."
    },
    {
      "at": 6.4,
      "text": "Probe the new middle: index 5 holds 31, which is larger than 23."
    },
    {
      "at": 8.8,
      "text": "That discards 31 and everything to its right, so hi drops to index 4. One cell is left: index 4."
    },
    {
      "at": 10.8,
      "text": "Probe it: 23. The midpoint is the answer only now, after the window has closed on it."
    },
    {
      "at": 12.8,
      "text": "Three probes for seven cells. The window halved each step, and at no point did it exclude the target."
    }
  ],
  "fallback": {
    "text": "Static trace table for the sorted array [3, 8, 12, 19, 23, 31, 40] and target 23. Row 1: lo=0, hi=6, mid=3, a[3]=19, 19 is less than 23 so lo becomes 4; window 7 cells wide containing indices 0..6. Row 2: lo=4, hi=6, mid=5, a[5]=31, 31 is greater than 23 so hi becomes 4; window 3 cells wide containing 4..6. Row 3: lo=4, hi=4, mid=4, a[4]=23, found. Each row shades the surviving window and marks that 23 sits inside every shaded window: 3 probes, window widths 7, 3, 1."
  },
  "accessibility": {
    "alt": "A row of seven sorted numbers with a shaded rectangle over the cells that can still contain 23. A blue arrow above the window marks the midpoint, and 'lo' and 'hi' labels sit under the window edges. The window slides inward after each comparison, and a dashed red ring around 23 shows the target never leaving it until the window is that one cell.",
    "reducedMotion": "Show the three trace rows side by side: for each row the shaded window, the labelled midpoint value, and the comparison result. The final row is the single cell holding 23.",
    "keyboard": true
  },
